OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1786198692
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G2/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Thu 13 Aug to Sat 22 Aug
OL,6,FSomething of a north to south split to
OL,7,Fstart the period. Some rain or showers
OL,8,Fare likely in the north whilst it will
OL,9,Fbe predominantly dry, sunny and hot in
OL,10,Fthe south. The heat in the south will
OL,11,Flikely ease into next weekend but
OL,12,Fprobably remain a little above
OL,13,Faverage. Further into August high
OL,14,Fpressure will likely become more
OL,15,Fwidely dominant leading to settled
OL,16,Fconditions for most. There are signs
OL,17,Fthat low pressure systems or thundery
OL,18,Finterludes will interrupt this at
OL,19,Ftimes, but rainfall amounts will
OL,20,Fprobably be variable, with some areas
OL,21,Fcontinuing to see relatively little.
OL,22,FTemperatures are likely to remain
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,23,Fabove average, with a chance of a
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
OL,24,Freturn of the hot conditions seen
OL,25,Fearlier in the period.
FL,164,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16303
SC,0003
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F163A1786198692
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G3/3
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GUK long range forecast
OL,4,
OL,5,COutlook for Sun 23 Aug to Sun 6 SepFThe
OL,6,Fbroad theme of high pressure remaining
OL,7,Fin place at least close to the UK
OL,8,Fseems most probable, but with
OL,9,Foccasional more unsettled or
OL,10,Fchangeable interludes. These
OL,11,Finterludes will either be the result
OL,12,Fof Atlantic frontal systems moving
OL,13,Feast or thundery plumes possibly
OL,14,Fdrifting north from the continent. The
OL,15,Fbroadly settled conditions mean that
OL,16,Frainfall amounts overall are more
OL,17,Flikely to be below normal than above.
OL,18,FTemperatures will probably be above
OL,19,Faverage and some spells of hot weather
OL,20,Fand heatwaves are possible, especially
OL,21,Fin the south.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
